 "sections": [
  {
   "id": 6,
   "kind": "notes",
   "report": true,
   "open": true,
   "name": "Protocol",
   "html": "<h2>BCA protein assay, 562 nm</h2><p>Protein reduces Cu\u00b2\u207a to Cu\u207a, which forms a purple complex with bicinchoninic acid (562 nm). Typical microplate format: 25 \u00b5l of standard or sample plus 200 \u00b5l of working reagent, 30 minutes at 37 \u00b0C. Follow your kit's instructions.</p><p>The workflow warms the chamber to 37 \u00b0C, incubates, then switches the incubator off before reading.</p><p><b>Layout.</b> Standards in rows A\u2013G of columns 1\u20132 (duplicates); buffer blanks in H1\u2013H2, subtracted from every well. Unknowns in duplicate pairs of columns 3\u201312 (Un01 \u2026 Un40); change the template to match your plate.</p><p><b>Results.</b> The Unknowns table interpolates each well on the standard curve (quadratic fit). Adj.Result multiplies by the dilution factor. Values outside the standards are flagged.</p><p><b>Workflow.</b> Run it from the Workflow section to have the reader shake, incubate and read; or just press Read when the plate is ready.</p>",
   "summaries": [],
   "show_formulas": false
  },
  {
   "id": 1,
   "kind": "plate",
   "report": true,
   "open": true,
   "name": "BCA",
   "settings": {
    "mode": "endpoint",
    "wavelengths": [
     562
    ],
    "run_time": 300,
    "interval": 30,
    "first_col": 1,
    "last_col": 12,
    "mix_before": false,
    "mix_before_s": 5,
    "mix_between": false,
    "mix_between_s": 3,
    "autocalibrate": true,
    "pre_read": false,
    "start": 350,
    "stop": 750,
    "step": 10,
    "delay": 0,
    "wait_temp": false,
    "columns": null
   },
